This branch addresses following comments from the bytedance
> Static Per-CPU Interrupt Allocation
> Dynamic IRTE Updates
> Interrupt Handling & Wakeup 

It introduces two static lists 'gappi_wakeup_list' and 'gappi_wakeup_list_lock'. 
Everytime there a vCPU unload it is appended on the per-CPU list of the
previous CPU on which it was running.  The IRTE is configured with the same
destination and vector "POSTED_INTR_WAKEUP_VECTOR".

The kvm_amd also registers a notification handler called
'avic_gappi_wakeup_handler'. When given CPU receives an GAPPI interrupt, this
handler iterates over the list of vCPUs assigned to that CPU and wakes the vCPU
if has a pending bit in IRR.

Advantages of this branch over the last one:
1) The number of GAPPI interrupts are always fixed instead of allocated
   dynamically when interrupt is allocated.
2) There is no need to call the affinity change interface when vCPU is
   migrated as every CPU has a static IDT entry called
   "POSTED_INTR_WAKEUP_VECTOR".
